          "claim": "Adding up to 2 incremental staff-hours per pilot café per weekday costs up to $60/store/day at the assumed $30/hour loaded rate, requiring 20 genuinely incremental transactions to break even before other costs. Whether those transactions materialize is unresolved this move (d.home.h6).",
          "cite": ["d.home.h6"]
        },
        {
          "link": "measurement_infrastructure_committed",
          "basis": "dossier_fact",
          "claim": "Attempt-to-purchase funnels, repeat-purchase cohorts, and paired-store baselines begin accumulating in January 2027. No completed pairs or cohorts exist at move-one close; kill-criteria gates remain unevaluated (d.home.h9).",
          "cite": ["d.home.h9"]
        }
      ],
      "kill_criteria": ["service", "economics", "retention"],
      "outcome": {
        "description": "Pilot operational structure is established. Capacity reservation is active in principle; effective slot cap awaits measured baselines. Instrumentation is deployed. No kill criterion is evaluable at move-one close: complete_store_pairs remains 0 and cohorts are not yet complete.",
        "board_delta": {
          "calendar_period": "January 2027",
          "pilot_cafes": 50,
          "comparison_cafes": 50,
          "cafe_capacity_reservation_pct": 20,
          "complete_store_pairs": 0,
          "pilot_cohort_complete_customers": 0,
          "comparison_cohort_complete_customers": 0,
          "measured_capacity_per_15min": null,
          "adjusted_cafe_wait_reduction_pct": null,
          "incremental_daily_contribution_usd": null,
          "mobile_repeat_change_pp": null,
          "public_strategy_history": [
            "Move 1 — Starbucks: Launched 50-café peak-time capacity-reservation pilot (20% reserved for café orders, 07:00–10:00 weekdays) with matched 50-comparison-café instrumentation. No baseline measurements yet complete."
          ]
        },
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      "branches": null
    },
    {
      "ruling_id": "r2_buyer_response_to_pilot",
      "basis": "judgment",
      "rationale": "Three buyer segments commit distinct contingent behaviors (m1.buyer.a1, m1.buyer.a2, m1.buyer.a3). Their triggers depend on offered pickup times, which depend on the slot cap, which depends on measured baseline capacity — none of which is resolved at move-one close. I adjudicate the structural mechanism by segment; I declare a branch on whether mobile-slot pressure is sufficient in January to trigger switching thresholds, because actual capacity baselines and daily demand distributions are unknown (d.buyer.b3, d.buyer.b8). No segment weights or switching probabilities exist in the record; I preserve those fields as null.",
