          "public_strategy_history": [
            "Move 1 — Starbucks: Launched 50-café peak-time capacity-reservation pilot (20% reserved for café orders, 07:00–10:00 weekdays) with matched 50-comparison-café instrumentation. No baseline measurements yet complete.",
            "Move 1 — Buyer: Habitual-app and commuter segments adopt contingent switching rules; walk-in segment unaffected. Switching triggers are active but outcomes depend on slot pressure not yet measurable.",
            "Move 1 — Dutch Bros: Added 20 labor hours/week per shop at 12 shops for 07:00–10:00 peak (Jan 1). In-app and social campaign with $1 Order Ahead credit for first-time users, capped at 100/shop, running Jan 15–31.",
            "Move 1 — Dunkin: Launched $6 breakfast Meal Deal mobile bundle at 15 consenting franchise locations near Starbucks pilot cafés, with local marketing campaign. Combined promotion-and-staffing spend capped at $20,000 for January. One-month economics review with exit rule committed."
          ]
        },
